Simple ROS2 node that publishes LaserScan messages from a Radar_MB_1R2T_V1.5.9 lidar module.
One message is published per full revolution.

Build using 'colcon build' from the workspace root
Run with 'ros2 run lidar_testnode lidar'

Parameters (set with --ros-args -p name:=value):
  port             serial port (default /dev/ttyUSB0)
  baudrate         serial baud rate (default 153600)
  topic            topic to publish on (default /lidar_mb_1r2t/scan)
  frame_id         frame of the published scans (default lidar_frame)
  range_min        minimum valid range in metres (default 0.01)
  range_max        maximum valid range in metres (default 20.0)
  verify_checksum  drop packets whose checksum does not match (default false)

The two header bytes after the stop angle are assumed to be a checksum, but
this has not been confirmed. A few seconds after starting, the node logs how
many packets matched the assumed checksum. If (nearly) all of them match, it is
safe to enable verify_checksum.

Run the parser unit tests with 'colcon test --packages-select lidar_testnode'
or with 'python3 -m pytest test/test_protocol.py' from src/lidar_testnode.
